      "content": "That makes sense. But I want to make sure the data doesn't get too messy. When you say \"demographic volatility,\" how should the model actually distinguish between \"healthy\" diversity/change and the kind of \"volatility\" that actually signals a risk of unrest? Like, if a neighborhood is seeing a huge influx of a specific ethnic group or a shift in the racial makeup, should the algorithm treat that as a high-risk indicator for instability?",
